{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "NTiedtkeParameters",
    "description": "Scheme constants of WRF's New Tiedtke mass-flux convection scheme (`cu_physics = 16`), transcribed from the `cu_ntiedtke_common` module of `phys/physics_mmm/cu_ntiedtke.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `cu_ntiedtke_run`). Mounted by every New Tiedtke component as subsystem `par`, so that no tuning constant is written inline in the physics.\n\nTHE VALUES ARE THE SCHEME'S, NOT THE SOURCE'S DECIMALS. Every constant in `cu_ntiedtke_common` is declared `real(kind=kind_phys), parameter` but INITIALISED FROM A DEFAULT-REAL LITERAL, so a `kind_phys = real64` build runs the binary64 widening of the literal's binary32 value -- the defect FORTRAN_BUGS N2 records for YSU and WSM6, N103 for GWDO, and N109 for this scheme. The count below covers `cu_ntiedtke_common`; the same defect runs through the routines' own inline literals, and the ones this repository has needed so far (cuadjtqn's second-step threshold, cuflxn's evaporation and melting constants, cuentrn's sub-cloud detrainment rate) are carried here too, at their roundings. Ten of the MODULE's literals are not exactly representable in binary32, and the numbers below are their roundings: `tmelt` = 273.1600036621094, `c1es` = 610.780029296875, `c3les` = 17.26938819885254, `c4les` = 35.86000061035156, `c4ies` = 7.659999847412109, `entrdd` = 0.00019999999494757503, `cmfcmin` = 1.000000013351432e-10, `cmfdeps` = 0.30000001192092896, `cprcon` = 0.00139999995008111, `pgcoef` = 0.699999988079071. `tmelt` and the four Magnus coefficients sit inside the exponent of the saturation vapour pressure, where a 1.3e-8 shift in `tmelt` alone moves q_sat by 2.6e-7 relative -- two orders above the rel 1e-9 contract -- so this is not a cosmetic choice.\n\nThe SEVEN constants the scheme does NOT declare -- cp, R_d, R_v, L_v, L_s, L_f and g -- arrive as ARGUMENTS of `cu_ntiedtke_init`, which derives ten more from them. Those come from `lib/wrf_constants.esm` at full binary64 precision, because an argument can be supplied at full precision whereas an internal literal cannot; the derived ten are equations here rather than numbers, so they follow whatever the mounting document's constants are.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "wrf",
      "convection",
      "cumulus",
      "new-tiedtke",
      "scheme-constants"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Tiedtke, M. (1989). A comprehensive mass flux scheme for cumulus parameterization in large-scale models. Mon. Wea. Rev. 117, 1779-1800.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(1989)117<1779:ACMFSF>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Zhang, C., Y. Wang, and K. Hamilton (2011). Improved representation of boundary layer clouds over the southeast Pacific in ARW-WRF using a modified Tiedtke cumulus parameterization scheme. Mon. Wea. Rev. 139, 3489-3513.",
        "doi": "10.1175/MWR-D-10-05091.1"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics cu_ntiedtke.F90 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule), module cu_ntiedtke_common."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "NTiedtkeParameters": {
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "t13": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.3333333432674408,
          "description": "One third, as the scheme holds it: `1.0/3.0` evaluated in default real and widened. Used as the exponent of the cube root in the updraught's precipitation conversion."
        },
        "tmelt": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 273.1600036621094,
          "description": "Triple-point temperature, the reference of the Magnus saturation-vapour-pressure formula. Written `273.16` in default real; the 3.7e-3 K difference from that decimal shifts q_sat by 2.6e-7 relative through the exponent (N109)."
        },
        "c1es": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "default": 610.780029296875,
          "description": "Saturation vapour pressure at the triple point (written 610.78)."
        },
        "c3les": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 17.26938819885254,
          "description": "Magnus numerator coefficient over WATER (written 17.2693882)."
        },
        "c3ies": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 21.875,
          "description": "Magnus numerator coefficient over ICE. Exactly representable in binary32, so it is the source decimal."
        },
        "c4les": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 35.86000061035156,
          "description": "Magnus denominator offset over WATER (written 35.86)."
        },
        "c4ies": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 7.659999847412109,
          "description": "Magnus denominator offset over ICE (written 7.66)."
        },
        "rtwat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Upper end of the mixed-phase range: at and above it the condensate is all liquid. The scheme sets it equal to tmelt."
        },
        "rtber": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Bergeron temperature, tmelt - 5 K. Declared in the common module; used by the updraught's freezing parameterisation."
        },
        "rtice": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Lower end of the mixed-phase range, tmelt - 23 K: at and below it the condensate is all ice."
        },
        "entrdd": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/m",
          "default": 0.00019999999494757503,
          "description": "Fractional entrainment rate of the downdraught (written 2.0e-4)."
        },
        "cmfcmax": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Maximum cloud-base mass flux."
        },
        "cmfcmin": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "default": 1.000000013351432e-10,
          "description": "Minimum cloud-base mass flux below which the convection is treated as absent (written 1.e-10)."
        },
        "cmfdeps": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.30000001192092896,
          "description": "Fraction of the cloud-base updraught mass flux that becomes the downdraught mass flux at the level of free sinking (written 0.30)."
        },
        "zdnoprc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "default": 20000.0,
          "description": "Minimum cloud depth in pressure for precipitation to be generated: a cloud shallower than 200 hPa makes none."
        },
        "cprcon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/m",
          "default": 0.00139999995008111,
          "description": "Conversion rate from cloud water to precipitation per unit height (written 1.4e-3)."
        },
        "pgcoef": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.699999988079071,
          "description": "Pressure-gradient coefficient of the convective momentum transport (written 0.7)."
        },
        "ztaumel": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 18000.0,
          "description": "Time scale over which falling snow melts once it is above the freezing level. Exactly representable in binary32."
        },
        "zcucov": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.05000000074505806,
          "description": "Fractional area of the grid cell the convective precipitation falls through, used to concentrate the evaporation into the raining fraction (written 0.05)."
        },
        "zcpecons": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0005440000074915588,
          "description": "Coefficient of the Kessler-type evaporation rate of falling precipitation, before division by g (written 5.44e-4)."
        },
        "evap_c1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.005090000107884407,
          "description": "Reference precipitation rate in the evaporation formula's power law (written 5.09e-3)."
        },
        "evap_expo": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5777000188827515,
          "description": "Exponent of the precipitation rate in the evaporation formula (written 0.5777)."
        },
        "rhevap_land": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.699999988079071,
          "description": "Relative humidity the sub-cloud layer is allowed to reach by evaporating precipitation, over LAND (written 0.7). The limit exists so that evaporation cannot saturate the sub-cloud layer in one step."
        },
        "rhevap_sea": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.8999999761581421,
          "description": "The same limit over water (written 0.9)."
        },
        "prec_min": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "default": 9.99999968265523e-21,
          "description": "Precipitation flux below which the evaporation sweep treats the column as dry and zeroes the flux outright (written 1.e-20)."
        },
        "detr_subcloud": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/m",
          "default": 7.500000356230885e-05,
          "description": "Fractional detrainment rate of the updraught below cloud base, the one surviving output of `cuentrn` (written 0.75e-4). Its companion, the turbulent entrainment, is structurally zero -- see FORTRAN_BUGS N112."
        },
        "qmax": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Cap on the saturation mixing ratio inside the moist adjustment, `zqmax = 0.5` of cuadjtqn. A local of that routine rather than a module constant, but a tuning number all the same, so it lives here. Exactly representable in binary32."
        },
        "zcond_eps": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "default": 9.99999968265523e-21,
          "description": "Threshold below which the moist adjustment discards its SECOND Newton step: cuadjtqn's inline `if (abs(zcond) < 1.e-20)`. A default-real literal like the rest (N109), so the scheme runs 9.99999968265523e-21. It guards against refining a correction that is already at the resolution of the mixing ratio."
        },
        "momtrans": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 2.0,
          "description": "Convective momentum transport option: 1 the original Tiedtke transport, 2 the Gregory et al. (1997) form with the pressure-gradient term. The scheme fixes it at 2."
        },
        "nonequil": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when the deep closure uses the non-equilibrium CAPE relaxation rather than the moisture-convergence closure. Fixed `.true.` in the scheme; carried as 0/1 because esm variables are real-valued."
        },
        "lmfpen": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when penetrative (deep) convection is allowed. Fixed `.true.`."
        },
        "lmfmid": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when mid-level convection is allowed. Fixed `.true.`."
        },
        "lmfscv": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when shallow convection is allowed. Fixed `.true.`."
        },
        "lmfdd": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when downdraughts are allowed. Fixed `.true.`."
        },
        "lmfdudv": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1 when the scheme transports momentum. Fixed `.true.`."
        },
        "rcpd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "(kg*K)/J",
          "description": "Reciprocal of the specific heat at constant pressure, 1/cp."
        },
        "c2es": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "c1es R_d / R_v: the saturation vapour pressure at the triple point already converted into a saturation MIXING RATIO numerator, so that q_sat = c2es exp(...) / p."
        },
        "c5les": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "c3les (tmelt - c4les), the numerator of the water-phase Clausius-Clapeyron derivative."
        },
        "c5ies": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "c3ies (tmelt - c4ies), the ice-phase counterpart."
        },
        "r5alvcp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K^2",
          "description": "c5les L_v / cp: the coefficient of the water-phase term of `foedem`, the derivative of q_sat with respect to temperature scaled by L/cp."
        },
        "r5alscp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K^2",
          "description": "c5ies L_s / cp, the ice-phase counterpart."
        },
        "ralvdcp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "L_v / cp, the temperature rise per unit condensed water mixing ratio for liquid."
        },
        "ralsdcp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "L_s / cp, the same for deposition to ice."
        },
        "ralfdcp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "L_f / cp, the temperature rise per unit freezing."
        },
        "vtmpc1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "R_v/R_d - 1, the virtual-temperature coefficient."
        },
        "zrg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s^2/m",
          "description": "1/g."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "rtwat",
          "rhs": "tmelt"
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rtber",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "tmelt",
              5.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rtice",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "tmelt",
              23.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rcpd",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1.0,
              "wrf.cp"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "c2es",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "c1es",
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "wrf.r_d",
                  "wrf.r_v"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "c5les",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "c3les",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "tmelt",
                  "c4les"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "c5ies",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "c3ies",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "tmelt",
                  "c4ies"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "r5alvcp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "c5les",
              "wrf.xlv",
              "rcpd"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "r5alscp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "c5ies",
              "wrf.xls",
              "rcpd"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ralvdcp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.xlv",
              "rcpd"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ralsdcp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.xls",
              "rcpd"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "ralfdcp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.xlf",
              "rcpd"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "vtmpc1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "wrf.r_v",
                  "wrf.r_d"
                ]
              },
              1.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zrg",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1.0,
              "wrf.g"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
